The notebook is in the shape of a rectangle, so you use the formulae for the perimeter of a rectangle.

$$
\begin{align}
P  & = 2l + 2b\\
& {= 2 \times 25 + 2 \times 15}\\
& {= \text{50} + \ \text{30}}\\
& {= \text{80}\ \text{cm}}
 \end{align}
$$

The notebook has a perimeter of 80 cm.

Use the formula for the area of a rectangle.

$$
\begin{align}
A  & = l \times b\\
& {= 25 \times 15}\\
& {= \text{375}\ \text{cm}^{2}}
 \end{align}
$$

The notebook has an area of 375 cm$^{2}$.

The window is in the shape of a square, so use the formula for the perimeter of a square.

$$
\begin{align}
P  & = 4s \\
& {= 4 \times 65}\\
& {= \text{260}\ \text{cm}}
 \end{align}
$$

The perimeter of the window is 260 cm, so the velvet strip will be 260 cm long.

Use the formula for area of a square.

$$
\begin{align}
A & = s^{2} \\
& {= 65 \times 65}\\
& {= 4,\!225\ \text{cm}^{2}}
\end{align}
$$

The blind will be 4,225 cm$^{2}$.
